    <item>
      <title>Diagrams with Mermaid</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/posts/2026/05/23/diagrams-with-mermaid/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 23 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/2026/05/23/diagrams-with-mermaid/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Most of the diagrams I want in a blog post are small — a flow, a sequence, the shape of a state machine. Reaching for Figma or draw.io for these is overkill. Mermaid lets me write them in the same fenced code blocks I already use for code.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;flowchart&#34;&gt;Flowchart&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The publish path for a post in this repo:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre class=&#34;mermaid&#34;&gt;flowchart LR&#xA;    Draft[Draft in Markdown] --&amp;gt; Commit[git commit]&#xA;    Commit --&amp;gt; Build[task build]&#xA;    Build --&amp;gt; Backstop{Backstop diff?}&#xA;    Backstop -- clean --&amp;gt; Deploy[Deploy]&#xA;    Backstop -- regression --&amp;gt; Fix[Fix and re-run]&#xA;    Fix --&amp;gt; Build&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;sequence&#34;&gt;Sequence&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;A request through the dev stack:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Style Guide</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/styleguide/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 12 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/styleguide/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;This page demonstrates every visual element defined in &lt;code&gt;DESIGN.md&lt;/code&gt;. If you change a token or a component, check this page renders correctly before merging.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;typography&#34;&gt;Typography&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;h1 id=&#34;heading-1--vt323-40px&#34;&gt;Heading 1 — VT323, 40px&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;heading-2--ibm-plex-sans-24px&#34;&gt;Heading 2 — IBM Plex Sans, 24px&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;heading-3--ibm-plex-sans-20px&#34;&gt;Heading 3 — IBM Plex Sans, 20px&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;h4 id=&#34;heading-4--ibm-plex-sans-18px-muted&#34;&gt;Heading 4 — IBM Plex Sans, 18px, muted&lt;/h4&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Body copy is set in &lt;strong&gt;Raleway&lt;/strong&gt; at 18px / 1.7 line-height. The point of this paragraph is to give you a long enough stretch of text to feel the reading rhythm. &lt;em&gt;Italics&lt;/em&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;bold&lt;/strong&gt; should sit comfortably inside the run without jumping out, and a &lt;a href=&#34;#&#34;&gt;link looks like this&lt;/a&gt; — the only saturated color in the system.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>A tiny state machine in Go</title>
