      <pubDate>Wed, 22 Apr 2026 11:30:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/2026/04/22/a-tiny-state-machine-in-go/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Every few months I reach for a state-machine library and then talk myself out of it. The reason is always the same: the thing I&amp;rsquo;m modeling has six states and twelve transitions, and a map literal is shorter than the import statement.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Here&amp;rsquo;s what I keep coming back to.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;the-shape&#34;&gt;The shape&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;A state machine is, at its smallest, a function from &lt;code&gt;(state, event) → state&lt;/code&gt;. Everything else is sugar. In Go that becomes:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Things I learned this week</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/posts/2026/03/18/things-i-learned-this-week/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 18 Mar 2026 16:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/2026/03/18/things-i-learned-this-week/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Every week I keep a running list of &amp;ldquo;huh, didn&amp;rsquo;t know that&amp;rdquo; moments. Most of them are small. Here&amp;rsquo;s this week&amp;rsquo;s, in the order I bumped into them.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;hugo-output-formats-dont-hot-reload&#34;&gt;Hugo output formats don&amp;rsquo;t hot-reload&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;If you add a new output format to &lt;code&gt;hugo.toml&lt;/code&gt;, the dev server won&amp;rsquo;t pick it up live. You have to restart &lt;code&gt;hugo server&lt;/code&gt;. I spent fifteen minutes wondering why &lt;code&gt;/llms.txt&lt;/code&gt; was 404ing before I remembered that.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;safejs-is-required-for-json-ld&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;safeJS&lt;/code&gt; is required for JSON-LD&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Go&amp;rsquo;s &lt;code&gt;html/template&lt;/code&gt; will happily JS-escape the JSON you put inside a &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;script&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; tag, turning your object into a quoted string. You have to pipe through &lt;code&gt;safeJS&lt;/code&gt; after &lt;code&gt;jsonify&lt;/code&gt; so the runtime treats the output as already-safe JavaScript.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>A short note on naming things</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/posts/2026/02/03/a-short-note-on-naming-things/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 03 Feb 2026 09:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/2026/02/03/a-short-note-on-naming-things/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The longer I write code, the more I think the best names are the ones nobody will quote at a conference. &lt;code&gt;count&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;result&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;item&lt;/code&gt;. Short, accurate, forgettable. The reader&amp;rsquo;s attention is finite, and every clever name spends some of it.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Save the inventive names for the places where the concept is genuinely new — a module, a public function, a domain term. Inside a function, you almost never need a thesaurus. You need a noun and a context, and the context is the function itself.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>WebGL with three.js</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/posts/2024/01/25/webgl-with-three.js/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 25 Jan 2024 10:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/2024/01/25/webgl-with-three.js/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;This is an example post demonstrating the new frontmatter structure compatible with Jekyll posts.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;features-demonstrated&#34;&gt;Features Demonstrated&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This post shows how the Hugo theme now supports:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;description&lt;/strong&gt;: A description field that appears in both the post and listings&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;canonical&lt;/strong&gt;: Link to the original publication URL&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;category&lt;/strong&gt;: Post categorization&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;tags&lt;/strong&gt;: Multiple tags for organizing content&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;assets&lt;/strong&gt;: Arrays for page-specific CSS and JavaScript files&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;assets-array&#34;&gt;Assets Array&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The assets array allows you to include additional CSS and JavaScript files on a per-post basis:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Typography, Fonts, and Why Monospace Headings Work So Well for Developer Blogs</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/posts/2024/01/20/typography-fonts-and-why-monospace-headings-work-so-well-for-developer-blogs/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 20 Jan 2024 14:30:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/2024/01/20/typography-fonts-and-why-monospace-headings-work-so-well-for-developer-blogs/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Here&amp;rsquo;s another post to show how multiple posts look in the theme.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The Frobiovox theme uses:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;VT323 font for the site name and navigation&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Cutive Mono for headings&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Raleway for body text&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This is a blockquote example showing the styling with a gray left border.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;why-monospace-for-headings&#34;&gt;Why Monospace for Headings?&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Monospace fonts carry a strong association with terminals, editors, and technical precision. Using one for headings on a developer blog signals intent — this is a place where code is taken seriously. The fixed character width also gives headings a calm, grid-like rhythm that pairs well with variable-width body text.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Getting Started with the Frobiovox Theme for Hugo Static Sites</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/posts/2024/01/15/getting-started-with-the-frobiovox-theme-for-hugo-static-sites/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 15 Jan 2024 10:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/2024/01/15/getting-started-with-the-frobiovox-theme-for-hugo-static-sites/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;This is an example blog post to demonstrate the Frobiovox theme for Hugo.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;features&#34;&gt;Features&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The theme includes:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Clean, minimal design&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Responsive layout&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Syntax highlighting for code&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&amp;ldquo;Read More&amp;rdquo; buttons on post listings&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;code-example&#34;&gt;Code Example&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Here&amp;rsquo;s a Python script that fetches posts from the Hugo content directory and prints a summary of each one, including title, date, and word count.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-python&#34; data-lang=&#34;python&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; os&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; re&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; datetime &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; datetime&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; pathlib &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; Path&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; typing &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; Optional&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;CONTENT_DIR &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; Path(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;content/posts&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;DATE_FORMAT &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;%Y-%m-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;%d&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;T%H:%M:%S%z&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;parse_frontmatter&lt;/span&gt;(text: str) &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; dict[str, str]:&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;&amp;#34;&amp;#34;Extract YAML frontmatter key-value pairs from a Hugo markdown file, ignoring nested arrays.&amp;#34;&amp;#34;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;match&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; re&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;match&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;^---\n(.*?)\n---&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;, text, re&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;DOTALL)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;not&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;match&lt;/span&gt;:&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; {}&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    fields: dict[str, str] &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; {}&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; line &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;in&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;match&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;group(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;)&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;splitlines():&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;: &amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;in&lt;/span&gt; line &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;and&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;not&lt;/span&gt; line&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;startswith(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;  &amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;) &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;and&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;not&lt;/span&gt; line&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;startswith(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;\t&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;):&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;            key, _, value &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; line&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;partition(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;: &amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;            fields[key&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;strip()] &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; value&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;strip()&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;strip(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#39;&amp;#34;&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;)&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;strip(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;&amp;#39;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; fields&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;word_count&lt;/span&gt;(text: str) &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; int:&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;&amp;#34;&amp;#34;Count words in the body of a markdown file, stripping frontmatter and fenced code blocks.&amp;#34;&amp;#34;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    body &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; re&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;sub(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;^---.*?---\n&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;, text, flags&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;re&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;DOTALL)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    body &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; re&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;sub(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;```.*?```&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;, body, flags&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;re&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;DOTALL)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; len(body&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;split())&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;format_date&lt;/span&gt;(raw: str) &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; str:&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;try&lt;/span&gt;:&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; datetime&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;strptime(raw[:&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;19&lt;/span&gt;], &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;%Y-%m-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;%d&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;T%H:%M:%S&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;)&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;strftime(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;%b &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;%d&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;, %Y&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;except&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;ValueError&lt;/span&gt;:&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; raw[:&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;10&lt;/span&gt;]&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;results &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; []&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; md_file &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;in&lt;/span&gt; sorted(CONTENT_DIR&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;glob(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;*.md&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;), key&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;lambda&lt;/span&gt; f: f&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;stat()&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;st_mtime, reverse&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;True&lt;/span&gt;):&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    content &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; md_file&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;read_text(encoding&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;utf-8&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    meta &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; parse_frontmatter(content)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    title &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; meta&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;get(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;title&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;, md_file&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;stem)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    date_str &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; format_date(meta&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;get(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;date&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;1970-01-01T00:00:00&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;))&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    words &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; word_count(content)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    draft &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; meta&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;get(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;draft&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;false&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;)&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;lower() &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;true&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    results&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;append((date_str, words, title, draft))&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; date_str, words, title, draft &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;in&lt;/span&gt; results:&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    status &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34; [DRAFT]&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; draft &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;else&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    print(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;date_str&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;words&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;gt;5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt; words  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;title&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;}{&lt;/span&gt;status&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;This theme is based on the design of &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.frobiovox.com&#34;&gt;www.frobiovox.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
